      "writtenOn": "2019-08-08T22:22:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve found that some vendors aren\u0027t even familiar with Git, never mind Gerrit. For them, I ended up writing an intro doc that takes the approach of \"here\u0027s the absolute basics, now run these commands to make a commit and upload a CL\". I\u0027m not sure that we should encourage quite such a low-understanding approach, but the Gerrit team have these public \"Concepts and Workflows\" presentations for Git [0] and Gerrit [1] which might be good to link to here.\n\n[0]: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1IQCRPHEIX-qKo7QFxsD3V62yhyGA9_5YsYXFOiBpgkk/edit\n[1]: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1C73UgQdzZDw0gzpaEqIC6SPujZJhqamyqO1XOHjH-uk/edit",
      "revId": "8bb547e74f0b8c6d821652f67da768e08ed557a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "504f070f_1b5410cd",
        "filename": "docs/fingerprint/fingerprint-dev-for-partners.md",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-09T17:01:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for those links. I agree that it\u0027s not ideal to have the basic commands, but practically speaking if they don\u0027t have experience with git, it\u0027s quite a hill to climb when combined with gerrit. In my case the vendor was familiar with git, so it wasn\u0027t an issue.\n\nCan you share the \"basic commands\" you provided, and I can add them?",
      "parentUuid": "3edbfa4b_ec9fe52b",
      "revId": "8bb547e74f0b8c6d821652f67da768e08ed557a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
